#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/printing/_index.adoc:292
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"For the easiest printing, choose a printer that supports PostScript(R).  "
"Printers that support `PCL` are the next preferred.  With package:print/"
"ghostscript9-base[], these printers can be used as if they understood "
"PostScript(R) natively.  Printers that support PostScript(R) or `PCL` "
"directly almost always support direct printing of plain `ASCII` text files "
"also."
msgstr "为获得最简单的打印体验，请选择支持 PostScript(R) 的打印机。其次推荐支持 `PCL` 的打印机。安装 package:print/ghostscript9-base[] 后，这些打印机可以像原生支持 PostScript(R) 一样使用。直接支持 PostScript(R) 或 `PCL` 的打印机几乎总是也支持直接打印纯 `ASCII` 文本文件。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/printing/_index.adoc:297
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Line-based printers like typical inkjets usually do not support "
"PostScript(R) or `PCL`.  They often can print plain `ASCII` text files.  "
"package:print/ghostscript9-base[] supports the PDLs used by some of these "
"printers.  However, printing an entire graphic-based page on these printers "
"is often very slow due to the large amount of data to be transferred and "
"printed."
msgstr "典型喷墨打印机等逐行打印机通常不支持 PostScript(R) 或 `PCL`。它们通常可以打印纯 `ASCII` 文本文件。package:print/ghostscript9-base[] 支持部分此类打印机使用的 PDL。不过，在这些打印机上打印整页图形通常非常缓慢，因为需要传输和打印的数据量很大。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/printing/_index.adoc:302
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Host-based printers are often more difficult to set up.  Some cannot be used "
"at all because of proprietary PDLs.  Avoid these printers when possible.  "
"The particular `PDL` used by various models of printers can be found at "
"http://www.openprinting.org/printers[]."
msgstr "基于主机的打印机通常更难设置。有些打印机使用专有 PDL，因而完全无法使用。请尽可能避免使用这类打印机。各种型号打印机所用的特定 `PDL` 可在 link:http://www.openprinting.org/printers[] 查找。"

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/printing/_index.adoc:304
#, no-wrap
msgid "Direct Printing"
msgstr "直接打印"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/printing/_index.adoc:308
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"For occasional printing, files can be sent directly to a printer device "
"without any setup.  For example, a file called [.filename]#sample.txt# can "
"be sent to a `USB` printer:"
msgstr "偶尔打印时，无需进行任何设置即可将文件直接发送到打印机设备。例如，可以将名为 [.filename]#sample.txt# 的文件发送到 `USB` 打印机："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/printing/_index.adoc:312
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# cp sample.txt /dev/unlpt0\n"
msgstr "# cp sample.txt /dev/unlpt0\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/printing/_index.adoc:315
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Direct printing to network printers depends on the abilities of the printer, "
"but most accept print jobs on port 9100, and man:nc[1] can be used with "
"them. To print the same file to a printer with the `DNS` hostname of "
"_netlaser_:"
msgstr "直接向网络打印机打印取决于打印机的功能，但大多数打印机都接受通过端口 9100 发送的打印作业，并且可以使用 man:nc[1]。要将同一文件打印到 `DNS` 主机名为 __netlaser__ 的打印机："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/printing/_index.adoc:319
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# nc netlaser 9100 < sample.txt\n"
msgstr "# nc netlaser 9100 < sample.txt\n"

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/printing/_index.adoc:322
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "LPD (Line Printer Daemon)"
msgstr "LPD（行式打印机守护进程）"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/printing/_index.adoc:326
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Printing a file in the background is called _spooling_.  A spooler allows "
"the user to continue with other programs on the computer without waiting for "
"the printer to slowly complete the print job."
msgstr "在后台打印文件称为__假脱机打印__。假脱机程序让用户无需等待打印机慢慢完成打印作业，就可以继续使用计算机上的其他程序。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/printing/_index.adoc:329
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"FreeBSD includes a spooler called man:lpd[8].  Print jobs are submitted with "
"man:lpr[1]."
msgstr "FreeBSD 包含一个名为 man:lpd[8] 的假脱机程序。使用 man:lpr[1] 提交打印作业。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/printing/_index.adoc:331
#, no-wrap
msgid "Initial Setup"
msgstr "初始设定"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/printing/_index.adoc:334
msgid ""
"A directory for storing print jobs is created, ownership is set, and the "
"permissions are set to prevent other users from viewing the contents of "
"those files:"
msgstr ""
"建立要用来储存打印工作的目录、设定拥有关系以及权限来避免其他使用者可以检视这"
"些文件的内容："

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/printing/_index.adoc:345
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Printers are defined in [.filename]#/etc/printcap#.  An entry for each "
"printer includes details like a name, the port where it is attached, and "
"various other settings.  Create [.filename]#/etc/printcap# with these "
"contents:"
msgstr ""
"印表机会定义在<filename>/etc/printcap</filename>，每台打印机项目所包含的详细"
"数据有名称、连接的接头以及各种其他设定。建立<filename>/etc/printcap</"
"filename>使用以下内容："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/printing/_index.adoc:354
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"lp:\\\t\t\t\t<.>\n"
"\t:lp=/dev/unlpt0:\\\t<.>\n"
"\t:sh:\\\t\t\t<.>\n"
"\t:mx#0:\\\t\t\t<.>\n"
"\t:sd=/var/spool/lpd/lp:\\\t<.>\n"
"\t:lf=/var/log/lpd-errs:\t<.>\n"
msgstr "lp:\\\t\t\t\t<.>\n\t:lp=/dev/unlpt0:\\\t<.>\n\t:sh:\\\t\t\t<.>\n\t:mx#0:\\\t\t\t<.>\n\t:sd=/var/spool/lpd/lp:\\\t<.>\n\t:lf=/var/log/lpd-errs:\t<.>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/printing/_index.adoc:357
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The name of this printer. man:lpr[1] sends print jobs to the `lp` printer "
"unless another printer is specified with `-P`, so the default printer should "
"be named `lp`."
msgstr "此打印机的名称。除非使用 `-P` 指定其他打印机，否则 man:lpr[1] 会将打印作业发送到 `lp` 打印机，因此默认打印机应命名为 `lp`。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/printing/_index.adoc:359
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The device where the printer is connected. Replace this line with the "
"appropriate one for the connection type shown here."
msgstr "打印机所连接到装置。替换此行为正确的联机类型，如此处所示。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/printing/_index.adoc:361
#, fuzzy
msgid "Suppress the printing of a header page at the start of a print job."
msgstr "在打印工作开始时不打印首页。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/printing/_index.adoc:363
#, fuzzy
msgid "Do not limit the maximum size of a print job."
msgstr "不限制打印工作的最大尺寸。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/printing/_index.adoc:365
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The path to the spooling directory for this printer. Each printer uses its "
"own spooling directory."
msgstr ""
"此打印机的缓冲（Spooling）目录路径，每台印表机会自己使用一个独立的缓冲"
"（Spooling）目录。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/printing/_index.adoc:367
#, fuzzy
msgid "The log file where errors on this printer will be reported."
msgstr "回报此打印机的错误的日志档。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/printing/_index.adoc:369
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"After creating [.filename]#/etc/printcap#, use man:chkprintcap[8] to test it "
"for errors:"
msgstr "创建 [.filename]#/etc/printcap# 后，使用 man:chkprintcap[8] 检查其中是否有错误："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/printing/_index.adoc:373
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# chkprintcap\n"
msgstr "# chkprintcap\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/printing/_index.adoc:376
msgid "Fix any reported problems before continuing."
msgstr "在继续之前修正任何回报的问题。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/printing/_index.adoc:378
#, fuzzy
msgid "Enable man:lpd[8] in [.filename]#/etc/rc.conf#:"
msgstr "在 [.filename]#/etc/rc.conf# 中启用 man:lpd[8]："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/printing/_index.adoc:389
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# service lpd start\n"
msgstr "# service lpd start\n"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/printing/_index.adoc:392
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Printing with man:lpr[1]"
msgstr "使用 man:lpr[1] 打印"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/printing/_index.adoc:397
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Documents are sent to the printer with `lpr`.  A file to be printed can be "
"named on the command line or piped into `lpr`.  These two commands are "
"equivalent, sending the contents of [.filename]#doc.txt# to the default "
"printer:"
msgstr ""
"文档将用 <command> lpr </command> 发送到打印机。要打印的文件可以在命令行上命"
"名，也可以通过管道到<command>lpr</command>中。这两个命令是等效的, 将 "
"<filename> doc.txt </filename> 的内容发送到默认打印机:"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/printing/_index.adoc:402
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"% lpr doc.txt\n"
"% cat doc.txt | lpr\n"
msgstr "% lpr doc.txt\n% cat doc.txt | lpr\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/printing/_index.adoc:406
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Printers can be selected with `-P`.  To print to a printer called _laser_:"
msgstr "可以使用 `-P` 选择打印机。要打印到名为 __laser__ 的打印机："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/printing/_index.adoc:410
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "% lpr -Plaser doc.txt\n"
msgstr "% lpr -Plaser doc.txt\n"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/printing/_index.adoc:413
#, no-wrap
msgid "Filters"
msgstr "过滤器"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/printing/_index.adoc:417
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "The examples shown so far have sent the contents of a text file directly "
#| "to the printer. As long as the printer understands the content of those "
#| "files, output will be printed correctly."
msgid ""
"The examples shown so far have sent the contents of a text file directly to "
"the printer.  As long as the printer understands the content of those files, "
"output will be printed correctly."
msgstr ""
"到目前为止显示的示例已将文本文件的内容直接发送到打印机。只要打印机理解这些文"
"件的内容，输出就会被正确打印。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/printing/_index.adoc:419
msgid ""
"Some printers are not capable of printing plain text, and the input file "
"might not even be plain text."
msgstr "有些打印机无法打印纯文本，输入文件甚至可能不是纯文本。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/printing/_index.adoc:423
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"_Filters_ allow files to be translated or processed.  The typical use is to "
"translate one type of input, like plain text, into a form that the printer "
"can understand, like PostScript(R) or `PCL`.  Filters can also be used to "
"provide additional features, like adding page numbers or highlighting source "
"code to make it easier to read."
msgstr "__过滤器__可以转换或处理文件。典型用途是将一种输入格式（如纯文本）转换为打印机能够理解的格式（如 PostScript(R) 或 `PCL`）。过滤器还可用于提供其他功能，例如添加页码或突出显示源代码，使其更易于阅读。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/printing/_index.adoc:427
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The filters discussed here are _input filters_ or _text filters_.  These "
"filters convert the incoming file into different forms.  Use man:su[1] to "
"become `root` before creating the files."
msgstr "此处讨论的过滤器是__输入过滤器__或__文本过滤器__。这些过滤器会将输入文件转换为其他格式。创建这些文件前，请使用 man:su[1] 切换到 `root` 身份。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/printing/_index.adoc:430
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Filters are specified in [.filename]#/etc/printcap# with the `if=` "
"identifier.  To use [.filename]#/usr/local/libexec/lf2crlf# as a filter, "
"modify [.filename]#/etc/printcap# like this:"
msgstr "在 [.filename]#/etc/printcap# 中使用 `if=` 标识符指定过滤器。要使用 [.filename]#/usr/local/libexec/lf2crlf# 作为过滤器，请按如下方式修改 [.filename]#/etc/printcap#："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/printing/_index.adoc:440
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"lp:\\\n"
"\t:lp=/dev/unlpt0:\\\n"
"\t:sh:\\\n"
"\t:mx#0:\\\n"
"\t:sd=/var/spool/lpd/lp:\\\n"
"\t:if=/usr/local/libexec/lf2crlf:\\   <.>\n"
"\t:lf=/var/log/lpd-errs:\n"
msgstr "lp:\\\n\t:lp=/dev/unlpt0:\\\n\t:sh:\\\n\t:mx#0:\\\n\t:sd=/var/spool/lpd/lp:\\\n\t:if=/usr/local/libexec/lf2crlf:\\   <.>\n\t:lf=/var/log/lpd-errs:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/printing/_index.adoc:443
#, fuzzy
msgid "`if=` identifies the _input filter_ that will be used on incoming text."
msgstr "`if=` 用于指定将应用于输入文本的__输入过滤器__。"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/printing/_index.adoc:448
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The backslash _line continuation_ characters at the end of the lines in [."
"filename]#printcap# entries reveal that an entry for a printer is really "
"just one long line with entries delimited by colon characters.  An earlier "
"example can be rewritten as a single less-readable line:"
msgstr ""
"printcap项中行尾的反斜杠行连续字符表明，打印机项实际上只是一个长行，其中的项"
"由冒号字符分隔。前面的示例可以重写为单个可读性较差的行："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/printing/_index.adoc:452
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid "lp:lp=/dev/unlpt0:sh:mx#0:sd=/var/spool/lpd/lp:if=/usr/local/libexec/lf2crlf:lf=/var/log/lpd-errs:\n"
msgstr "lp:lp=/dev/unlpt0:sh:mx#0:sd=/var/spool/lpd/lp:if=/usr/local/libexec/lf2crlf:lf=/var/log/lpd-errs:\n"

#. type: Title ====
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/printing/_index.adoc:457
#, no-wrap
msgid "Preventing Stairstepping on Plain Text Printers"
msgstr "避免在纯文字打印机阶梯状打印"

#. type: delimited block = 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/printing/_index.adoc:461
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Typical FreeBSD text files contain only a single line feed character at the "
"end of each line.  These lines will \"stairstep\" on a standard printer:"
msgstr "典型的 FreeBSD 文本文件只在每行末尾包含一个换行符。在标准打印机上，这些行会呈现“阶梯状”："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/printing/_index.adoc:467
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A printed file looks\n"
"                    like the steps of a staircase\n"
"                                                 scattered by the wind\n"
msgstr ""
"A printed file looks\n"
"                    like the steps of a staircase\n"
"                                                 scattered by the wind\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/printing/_index.adoc:472
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A filter can convert the newline characters into carriage returns and "
"newlines.  The carriage returns make the printer return to the left after "
"each line.  Create [.filename]#/usr/local/libexec/lf2crlf# with these "
"contents:"
msgstr ""
"过滤器可以将换行符转换为回车和换行符。回车使打印机在每行之后回到左边。用下列"
"内容创建<filename>/usr/local/libexec/lf2crlf</filename>："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/printing/_index.adoc:478
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
msgid ""
"#!/bin/sh\n"
"CR=$'\\r'\n"
"/usr/bin/sed -e \"s/$/${CR}/g\"\n"
msgstr ""
"#!/bin/sh\n"
"CR=$'\\r'\n"
"/usr/bin/sed -e \"s/$/${CR}/g\"\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/printing/_index.adoc:481
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/printing/_index.adoc:513
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/printing/_index.adoc:546
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/printing/_index.adoc:603
msgid "Set the permissions and make it executable:"
msgstr "设置可执行权限权限:"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/books/handbook/printing/_index.adoc:485
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "# chmod 555 /usr/local/libexec/lf2crlf\n"
msgstr "# chmod 555 /usr/local/libexec/lf2crlf\n"

